WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.494
[Michael]
<i> This is Iquitos, Peru,</i>

00:00:28.527 --> 00:00:31.330
the world's largest city
inaccessible by road.

00:00:31.363 --> 00:00:35.768
<i> The only way in and out
 is by air or by river,</i>

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:37.537
<i> the Amazon River.</i>

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.640
I'm about to head up the Amazon
to a remote jungle retreat

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:45.445
called Refugio Altiplano,
the Refuge on the Higher Plain.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.713
There, I will meet
with local shamans

00:00:47.746 --> 00:00:51.751
to drink an ancient
psychedelic drug, ayahuasca.

00:00:57.556 --> 00:01:01.561
Ayahuasca contains
dimethyltryptamine, DMT,

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.863
a molecule shaped
very similar to serotonin,

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:07.166
<i> a neurotransmitter
 in our brains.</i>

00:01:07.199 --> 00:01:10.269
Ingesting ayahuasca and flooding
the brain with DMT

00:01:10.302 --> 00:01:13.739
leads to what many describe
as spiritual experiences--

00:01:13.772 --> 00:01:15.374 line:0%
<i> strong, vivid visions,</i>

00:01:15.407 --> 00:01:18.578 line:0%
<i> a sense of oneness
 with the universe,</i>

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:22.148 line:0%
even a sense
of one's self dying.

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:24.750
But mystical,
magical language like that

00:01:24.783 --> 00:01:26.886
doesn't really seem relevant
to scientific inquiry.

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:29.889
It can often scare away those
who are scientifically minded.

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:32.592
However an understanding
of the human mind

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.360
isn't complete unless
it considers

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:36.863
everything the brain
is capable of.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:42.201
What does it mean to feel
at one with the universe?

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:44.904
Why should our brains even
be capable of such a feeling?

00:01:44.937 --> 00:01:48.741
This isn't about having fun
or taking a risk

00:01:48.774 --> 00:01:50.610
or doing something extreme.

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:54.180
I want to learn
what my mind is capable of.

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:56.916
I'm about to embark
on a journey.

00:01:56.949 --> 00:02:00.720
[theme music playing]

00:02:16.835 --> 00:02:19.238 line:0%
Psychedelics are chemicals

00:02:19.271 --> 00:02:22.241 line:0%
that are structurally similar
to neurotransmitters

00:02:22.274 --> 00:02:24.644
<i> already used by our brains.</i>

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:27.446 line:83%
<i> When we ingest them,
 they bind to receptors</i>

00:02:27.479 --> 00:02:29.515 line:83%
<i> and alter cognition
 and perception</i>

00:02:29.548 --> 00:02:32.451 line:83%
<i> in ways we're still trying
 to understand.</i>

00:02:32.484 --> 00:02:35.221
<i> When many people think
 of psychedelics,</i>

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:38.491
<i> they think about people
 challenging societal norms</i>

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:39.859
<i> and recreational
 thrill-seekers,</i>

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:41.861
<i> but that only attends</i>

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:45.865
<i> to a particularly narrow slice
 of human history and culture.</i>

00:02:45.898 --> 00:02:49.502
<i> Fossil records, cave drawings,
 and archaeological digs</i>

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:51.504
<i> have all provided evidence
 that humans</i>

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:53.773
<i> have been using
 psychedelic compounds</i>

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:57.843
<i> for thousands of years, and
 by "used," I don't just mean</i>

00:02:57.876 --> 00:02:59.512
<i> in the stereotypical
 "trip out" sense.</i>

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:00.913
[screaming]

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:02.815
For instance,
among the indigenous peoples

00:03:02.848 --> 00:03:06.285
of the Amazon rainforest,
psychedelics were and,

00:03:06.318 --> 00:03:09.889
in many places, still are
a normal, common,

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:12.458
and totally
mainstream experience.

00:03:12.491 --> 00:03:16.529
As a member of these groups,
believing psychedelics can heal,

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:19.932
give visions of the future,
and connect you with deities

00:03:19.965 --> 00:03:22.935
is not some weird
or New Age idea.

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:25.371
It's the way things are.

00:03:25.404 --> 00:03:27.673
<i> But when psychedelics
 became associated</i>

00:03:27.706 --> 00:03:30.276
<i> with certain
 counterculture movements,</i>

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:33.512
<i> the United States banned
 research on them in 1970.</i>

00:03:33.545 --> 00:03:36.482
<i> Most other countries followed
 suit shortly afterwards.</i>

00:03:36.515 --> 00:03:40.353
<i> From then on, testing on humans
 was essentially gone,</i>

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:43.589
but recently, restrictions
have begun to loosen up,

00:03:43.622 --> 00:03:44.824
and a few researchers
have started

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.692
to investigate these substances

00:03:46.725 --> 00:03:50.630
in what some have described
as a psychedelic renaissance.

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:52.798
<i> Research universities
 are conducting</i>

00:03:52.831 --> 00:03:54.967
<i> comprehensive studies
 on the beneficial effects</i>

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.436
<i> of psychedelics on addiction,
 depression,</i>

00:03:57.469 --> 00:03:58.871
<i> and cancer-related trauma.</i>

00:03:58.904 --> 00:04:01.874
By approaching
psychedelics scientifically,

00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:04.677
what we find could
fundamentally transform

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:07.313
our understanding
of the human mind.

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:14.887
[trimmer buzzing]

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:17.390
When I go to Peru,
I will be accompanied

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:20.026
by Dr. Robin Carhart Harris,
one of the first

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:22.295
British researchers
in over 40 years

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.463
to investigate the effects
of psychedelics

00:04:24.496 --> 00:04:26.032
on the human mind.

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:28.000
He and his colleagues
have found that psychedelics

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:30.936
don't increase brain activity,
as previously thought.

00:04:30.969 --> 00:04:34.874 line:0%
<i> Instead, they decrease activity
 in certain areas.</i>

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:36.709 line:0%
<i> And the greater the decrease,</i>

00:04:36.742 --> 00:04:38.477 line:0%
the greater
the reported feelings

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:43.549
of what is called
ego dissolution or ego death.

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:46.652
<i> Your ego is your self-identity.</i>

00:04:46.685 --> 00:04:50.323
<i> It's the part that separates
 you from everything else,</i>

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:53.526 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> the part
 that creates narratives about
 the outside world</i>

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:55.428
<i> and your story in it.</i>

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.897
When the ego dissolves,
your sensations

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:01.534
and feelings don't cease
like when you're unconscious.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:04.937
<i> Instead, your attachment
 to your identity does,</i>

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:09.041
<i> and all that's left
 is naked perception.</i>

00:05:09.074 --> 00:05:10.843
Ego dissolution is a concept

00:05:10.876 --> 00:05:13.612
that I find difficult
to wrap my head around,

00:05:13.645 --> 00:05:15.948
but people who take psychedelics
say that it can be

00:05:15.981 --> 00:05:18.584
an extremely
frightening experience,

00:05:18.617 --> 00:05:21.620
but also a profoundly
transformative one,

00:05:21.653 --> 00:05:23.456
<i> one that makes them feel
 more connected</i>

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:26.025
<i> to others and to nature.</i>

00:05:26.058 --> 00:05:29.428
Now, I knew that I might feel
ego dissolution on ayahuasca,

00:05:29.461 --> 00:05:30.996
so to make sure I was ready,

00:05:31.029 --> 00:05:33.032
I decided to speak
to some experts.

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:38.938
<i> Before setting off to Peru,
 Dr. Carhart Harris traveled</i>

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:41.574
<i> from Imperial College, London,
 to meet with me.</i>

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:43.642 align:start position:0% line:0%
This will be one
of the first times

00:05:43.675 --> 00:05:48.514 align:start position:0% line:0%
that anyone has scanned
a healthy person's brain

00:05:48.547 --> 00:05:52.618 align:start position:0% line:0%
with FMRI before
and after ayahuasca.

00:05:52.651 --> 00:05:56.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It's quite pioneering work,
really.

00:05:56.488 --> 00:05:59.125 align:start size:84% position:16%
The thing that's on my mind
right now is intention.

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:01.627
-Yeah.
-I've heard you should know why

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:03.929 align:start size:81% position:19%
you're drinking ayahuasca.

00:06:03.962 --> 00:06:06.832 align:start position:0%
Yeah, I would suggest
that you think

00:06:06.865 --> 00:06:09.101
about an emotional intention.

00:06:09.134 --> 00:06:12.838 align:start size:91% position:9%
To make it emotional is
a lot more frightening to me.

00:06:12.871 --> 00:06:14.940
-Yeah.
-Partly I think I'm quite happy,

00:06:14.973 --> 00:06:17.943 align:start size:63% position:38%
and I don't want
to ruin that, right?

00:06:17.976 --> 00:06:22.481 align:start size:66% position:34%
I don't want to drink
ayahuasca and then
think, "Oh, my gosh,

00:06:22.514 --> 00:06:24.884 align:start size:63% position:38%
I'm not close enough
to my mom,

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:27.553 align:start size:75% position:25%
or I don't show my wife
I appreciate her enough,

00:06:27.586 --> 00:06:29.655 align:start size:69% position:31%
and now
I just feel terrible."

00:06:29.688 --> 00:06:32.591 align:start position:0%
There's something to be said
for sitting with those thoughts,

00:06:32.624 --> 00:06:34.527 align:start size:88% position:13%
-being mindful of them.
-Right.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:38.464 align:start position:0%
And in so doing,
they become less of a threat.

00:06:38.497 --> 00:06:40.032 align:start size:91% position:9%
-Hmm.
-You look them in the eye.

00:06:40.065 --> 00:06:43.502 align:start position:0%
All of a sudden,
they reveal things to you,

00:06:43.535 --> 00:06:47.139 align:start position:0%
and their scariness
seems to dissipate.

00:06:47.172 --> 00:06:49.909 align:start size:78% position:22%
I hope I can embrace
that while I'm surrounded

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:52.945 align:start size:78% position:22%
by people who are
all filming me, you know?

00:06:52.978 --> 00:06:57.650 align:start position:0%
Yeah, the most important thing
is that intention to go in.

00:06:57.683 --> 00:07:00.019 align:start size:78% position:22%
-You dive in--
in and through.
-You don't resist.

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:02.021 align:start position:0%
You don't resist.

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:03.756 align:start size:66% position:34%
Yeah, I think that'll
really be important

00:07:03.789 --> 00:07:06.926 align:start size:69% position:31%
while I'm on the trip.

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:09.462
 [Michael]<i> Robin has
 arranged for a number
 of scientific tests</i>

00:07:09.495 --> 00:07:11.864
<i> to be done in order to measure
 brain activity,</i>

00:07:11.897 --> 00:07:13.499
<i> behavioral differences,</i>

00:07:13.532 --> 00:07:15.701
<i> and physiological changes
 to my brain.</i>

00:07:15.734 --> 00:07:17.703
[Robin]<i> Today, we are scanning
 Michael's brain</i>

00:07:17.736 --> 00:07:20.806
with functional magnetic
resonance imaging, or FMRI.

00:07:20.839 --> 00:07:23.609
<i> This allows us to see
 the whole brain</i>

00:07:23.642 --> 00:07:26.745
<i> and how different parts connect
 and talk to one another.</i>

00:07:26.778 --> 00:07:29.715
<i> This way, we can compare
 how Michael's brain may change</i>

00:07:29.748 --> 00:07:31.550
<i> before his experience
 with ayahuasca</i>

00:07:31.583 --> 00:07:34.019
to after
the ayahuasca experience.

00:07:34.052 --> 00:07:36.655
<i> I expect to see
 that one network of the brain</i>

00:07:36.688 --> 00:07:38.624
<i> that relates to introspection</i>

00:07:38.657 --> 00:07:41.861
<i> will become more strongly
 connected after the ayahuasca.</i>

00:07:46.298 --> 00:07:47.933
[Michael]
<i> After meeting Robin,</i>

00:07:47.966 --> 00:07:50.135
<i> I still felt some trepidation
 about my trip,</i>

00:07:50.168 --> 00:07:53.172
<i> but with my pre-ayahuasca
 FMRI completed,</i>

00:07:53.205 --> 00:07:55.475
<i> it was time to set off
 for Peru.</i>

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:01.247
<i> The trip to the Refugio
 Altiplano retreat</i>

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:04.884
<i> involved a flight
 to Lima, Peru,</i>

00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:07.753
<i> a second flight
 to Iquitos, Peru,</i>

00:08:07.786 --> 00:08:10.723
<i> followed by a 90-minute
 boat ride up the Amazon River.</i>

00:08:12.324 --> 00:08:14.793
<i> It was a long journey.</i>

00:08:14.826 --> 00:08:16.729
<i> And every minute I got closer</i>

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:18.598
<i> meant that it would be harder
 to turn back.</i>

00:08:20.699 --> 00:08:23.969
<i> The Refugio Altiplano retreat
 is in a very remote area</i>

00:08:24.002 --> 00:08:27.072
<i> of the Amazon River
 in the northern part of Peru,</i>

00:08:27.105 --> 00:08:29.808
<i> and I thought it would be
 a great setting</i>

00:08:29.841 --> 00:08:31.610
<i> for my ayahuasca experience.</i>

00:08:31.643 --> 00:08:35.080 align:start size:81% position:19%
So, Kelly, what does
the word "ayahuasca" mean?

00:08:35.113 --> 00:08:38.217 align:start position:0%
"Ayahuasca" means
the "vine of the soul."

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:42.021 align:start position:0% line:0%
Ayahuasca's been used
for possibly over 4,000 years

00:08:42.054 --> 00:08:45.057 align:start position:0% line:0%
in shamanic rituals
and is the primary

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:47.693 align:start position:0% line:0%
plant medicine
for healing in the villages.

00:08:50.896 --> 00:08:53.566
[Michael]<i> With the ayahuasca
 ceremony just hours away,</i>

00:08:53.599 --> 00:08:55.868
<i> I met with José,
 the shaman who would be</i>

00:08:55.901 --> 00:08:57.937
<i> my guide
 during this experience.</i>

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.838 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> -Hola, José, Claudia.
 -Hola, amigo.</i>

00:08:59.871 --> 00:09:01.040 align:start size:56% position:44%
[speaking Spanish]

00:09:02.808 --> 00:09:05.611 align:start position:0% line:0%
[speaking Spanish]

00:09:05.644 --> 00:09:07.846 align:start size:53% position:47% line:0%
[translating]
It's my pleasure
to have you here.

00:09:07.879 --> 00:09:10.182 line:0%
Welcome
to Refugio Altiplano,

00:09:10.215 --> 00:09:12.985 align:start size:69% position:31% line:0%
where many people come
to look for a change
in their lives.

00:09:13.018 --> 00:09:16.121 align:start size:56% position:44% line:0%
José, how do you
feel about someone
like me coming in,

00:09:16.154 --> 00:09:20.626 align:start size:53% position:47%
who is not part
of your culture,
taking part in it

00:09:20.659 --> 00:09:23.329 align:start size:69% position:31%
in a way
that might not come
from the same history?

00:09:23.362 --> 00:09:25.064 align:start position:0%
[speaking Spanish]

00:09:25.097 --> 00:09:26.799
[Claudia]
For me, there's no difference,

00:09:26.832 --> 00:09:29.168
and for the medicine,
it makes no difference.

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:32.972
This medicine, all it wants
is to make your life better

00:09:33.005 --> 00:09:34.239
and heal you.

00:09:34.272 --> 00:09:36.208
On the very first night
with our guests,

00:09:36.241 --> 00:09:39.378
we give them a very small
medicinal dose

00:09:39.411 --> 00:09:41.880
to see how each person's
gonna react differently

00:09:41.913 --> 00:09:43.882
to the medicine,
and then tomorrow night,

00:09:43.915 --> 00:09:46.619
we'll dial it up a little bit.

00:09:46.652 --> 00:09:48.721
[Michael]<i> It was great
 to speak with José</i>

00:09:48.754 --> 00:09:50.889
<i> about what the ceremony
 will entail.</i>

00:09:50.922 --> 00:09:53.792
<i> I am nervous about
 the emotional part of it,</i>

00:09:53.825 --> 00:09:55.828
and I'm nervous
about the visions and feeling

00:09:55.861 --> 00:09:57.897
like I've been disconnected
from the real world.

00:10:01.099 --> 00:10:04.269
<i> Scientists know very little
 about how ayahuasca works</i>

00:10:04.302 --> 00:10:06.972
<i> since its illegal status
 in many countries</i>

00:10:07.005 --> 00:10:08.707
<i> makes it difficult to study.</i>

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:10.676 line:0%
<i> We do know that
 its key ingredient</i>

00:10:10.709 --> 00:10:14.013 line:0%
<i> is dimethyltryptamine, or DMT,
 which is a hallucinogen</i>

00:10:14.046 --> 00:10:15.981
<i> thought to occur naturally
 in the human brain</i>

00:10:16.014 --> 00:10:17.783
<i> in small amounts.</i>

00:10:17.816 --> 00:10:21.053
<i> DMT can create
 psychoactive effects</i>

00:10:21.086 --> 00:10:24.056
<i> by acting on certain receptors
 in the brain.</i>

00:10:24.089 --> 00:10:29.228
<i>But normally, DMT is broken down
rapidly by enzymes in the brain.</i>

00:10:29.261 --> 00:10:33.232
<i> but ayahuasca is actually
 a brew made from two plants.</i>

00:10:33.265 --> 00:10:35.234 line:0%
<i> One contains DMT,</i>

00:10:35.267 --> 00:10:37.136 line:0%
<i> and the second contains
 a chemical inhibitor</i>

00:10:37.169 --> 00:10:39.905 line:0%
<i> that blocks our brain's ability
 to break down DMT,</i>

00:10:39.938 --> 00:10:43.042 line:0%
<i> allowing the effects to last
 as long as four hours.</i>

00:10:46.344 --> 00:10:49.214 line:0%
<i> Dr. Carhart Harris performed
 a series of tests on me</i>

00:10:49.247 --> 00:10:51.684 line:0%
<i> to compare how I change
 during this experience.</i>

00:10:51.717 --> 00:10:54.353 align:start size:78% position:22% line:0%
[Robin]
Given that we're in Peru,
we're in the jungle,

00:10:54.386 --> 00:10:58.123 align:start size:59% position:41%
and you're
drinking ayahuasca,
it has authenticity

00:10:58.156 --> 00:11:00.159 align:start size:56% position:44%
that perhaps
sometimes you lose

00:11:00.192 --> 00:11:02.928 align:start size:81% position:19%
when you give psychedelics
in the laboratory
environment.

00:11:02.961 --> 00:11:05.731 align:start size:84% position:16%
-Yeah.
-Because we're
going to be doing this

00:11:05.764 --> 00:11:10.235 size:88% position:56%
after you drink ayahuasca,
we need a control condition,

00:11:10.268 --> 00:11:12.805 align:start size:84% position:16%
so what I'm going to do now
is I'll ask you

00:11:12.838 --> 00:11:16.275 align:start size:78% position:22%
a short list of questions
about your journey here,

00:11:16.308 --> 00:11:19.878 align:start size:66% position:34%
and I want you
to rate how you feel
about these questions

00:11:19.911 --> 00:11:21.246 align:start size:50% position:50%
on a scale here.

00:11:21.279 --> 00:11:22.347 align:start size:66% position:34%
We have zero to nine.

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:24.216 size:88% position:56%
Nine will be strongly agree,

00:11:24.249 --> 00:11:27.119 align:start size:56% position:44%
and zero will be
strongly disagree.

00:11:27.152 --> 00:11:30.155 align:start size:63% position:38% line:0%
So "I learned more
from my journey here

00:11:30.188 --> 00:11:34.226 align:start size:69% position:31% line:0%
to this retreat center
about how past events

00:11:34.259 --> 00:11:36.495 align:start size:66% position:34% line:0%
have influenced
my present behavior."

00:11:36.528 --> 00:11:37.963 align:start position:0% line:0%
Two.

00:11:37.996 --> 00:11:40.866
-I got ideas areas during...
-Two.

00:11:40.899 --> 00:11:43.335
-Five. Six.
-Great.

00:11:43.368 --> 00:11:46.472
With different
psychedelic drugs to ayahuasca

00:11:46.505 --> 00:11:49.775
<i> like LSD and psilocybin,
 also DMT,</i>

00:11:49.808 --> 00:11:51.910
<i> we've found some quite
 consistent changes</i>

00:11:51.943 --> 00:11:53.479
in brain activity.

00:11:53.512 --> 00:11:55.514
<i> We've seen
 that the brain activity</i>

00:11:55.547 --> 00:11:57.416
<i> is richer and more varied.</i>

00:11:57.449 --> 00:12:00.285 line:0%
<i> Of course,
 we can't wheel an MRI scanner</i>

00:12:00.318 --> 00:12:03.489 line:0%
<i> up into the jungle,
 so the EEG setup that we have</i>

00:12:03.522 --> 00:12:05.824 line:0%
<i> is pretty much
 the best possibility</i>

00:12:05.857 --> 00:12:07.393 line:0%
<i> that we have to do this.</i>

00:12:10.128 --> 00:12:13.031
[Michael]
<i> According to Jose, this flower
 bath was meant</i>

00:12:13.064 --> 00:12:14.767
<i> to protect me from bad spirits
 during the ceremony. </i>

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:17.536 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
-[Michael speaks Spanish]
-[José chuckles]

00:12:17.569 --> 00:12:19.872
<i> I didn't believe in such
 things, but I was glad to do it</i>

00:12:19.905 --> 00:12:22.341
<i> because it was a symbol
 of José's good intentions.</i>

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:40.959
<i> Hola.
 Buenas noches.</i>

00:12:40.992 --> 00:12:43.962
[Michael]<i> The initial
 smaller-dose ceremony</i>

00:12:43.995 --> 00:12:46.131
<i> was expected to last
 about two hours</i>

00:12:46.164 --> 00:12:49.802
<i> with the effects beginning
 after 30 minutes.</i>

00:12:49.835 --> 00:12:53.138
[José speaking Spanish]

00:12:53.171 --> 00:12:57.576 align:start position:0%
We'll begin
with our ceremony tonight,
asking God to guide us,

00:12:57.609 --> 00:13:00.979 align:start position:0%
to give us knowledge
and intelligence.

00:13:01.012 --> 00:13:02.514 align:start size:72% position:28%
[José speaking Spanish]

00:13:02.547 --> 00:13:04.983 align:start position:0%
[Claudia]
We're going to bless
the medicine first.

00:13:05.016 --> 00:13:07.887
[music playing]

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:23.969 align:start position:0%
<i> Gracias.</i>

00:13:33.078 --> 00:13:35.214
[Michael]
<i> The ayahuasca tasted earthy.</i>

00:13:35.247 --> 00:13:36.949 align:start position:0% line:0%
[speaking Spanish]

00:13:36.982 --> 00:13:38.851
<i> Maybe also a bit like fennel
 or something.</i>

00:13:38.884 --> 00:13:40.319
<i> It's hard to say.</i>

00:13:40.352 --> 00:13:42.254
<i> I'd never tasted
 anything like it.</i>

00:13:42.287 --> 00:13:43.856 line:92%
<i> After swallowing it all,</i>

00:13:43.889 --> 00:13:45.891
<i> my heart started racing. </i>

00:13:45.924 --> 00:13:47.893
<i> It was the most nervous
 I would be all night.</i>

00:13:47.926 --> 00:13:50.996
<i> DMT from the ayahuasca
 was flowing</i>

00:13:51.029 --> 00:13:52.431
<i> into my blood and brain.</i>

00:13:52.464 --> 00:13:54.933
<i> There was no going back.</i>

00:13:54.966 --> 00:13:57.102
[José chanting]

00:14:04.509 --> 00:14:07.479
<i> Throughout the ceremony,
 shaman José is saying icaros,</i>

00:14:07.512 --> 00:14:10.082
<i> or chants,
 which were meant to guide me</i>

00:14:10.115 --> 00:14:11.984
<i> through my spiritual
 experience.</i>

00:14:12.017 --> 00:14:13.886
[chanting continues]

00:14:32.003 --> 00:14:35.007 align:start size:47% position:53% line:0%
[José chanting]

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:40.312
<i> The initial dose was meant
 to gently introduce me</i>

00:14:40.345 --> 00:14:41.914
<i> to ayahuasca.</i>

00:14:41.947 --> 00:14:44.283
<i> The effects began slowly
 and were mild.</i>

00:14:44.316 --> 00:14:46.184
<i> I began to feel
 as though the room</i>

00:14:46.217 --> 00:14:48.186
<i> were swinging like a cradle.</i>

00:14:48.219 --> 00:14:50.656
<i> I was aware that the motion
 wasn't really happening,</i>

00:14:50.689 --> 00:14:52.424
<i> but it made me feel sick</i>

00:14:52.457 --> 00:14:55.093
<i> and nervously off-balance
 nonetheless.</i>

00:14:55.126 --> 00:14:57.296
<i> My imagination was more vivid.</i>

00:14:57.329 --> 00:14:59.197
<i> Images in my mind
 were more detailed,</i>

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:01.166
<i> but almost always
 under my control.</i>

00:15:09.307 --> 00:15:12.277
<i> The ceremony ends when
 the shaman lights a candle.</i>

00:15:12.310 --> 00:15:14.613
<i> I was comforted by this
 because it was a sign</i>

00:15:14.646 --> 00:15:17.015
<i> that the effects would
 only be weakening from here.</i>

00:15:17.048 --> 00:15:18.517 align:start position:0%
Thank you, José.

00:15:21.086 --> 00:15:22.487 align:start position:0%
I think there were two moments
where I was actually

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:27.059 align:start position:0%
was surprised
by something that I saw.

00:15:27.092 --> 00:15:29.628 size:84% position:42%
One was like a very vivid--

00:15:29.661 --> 00:15:34.499
like bamboo that had been cut
so that it was at a slant,

00:15:34.532 --> 00:15:37.269 align:start position:0%
and I remember going,
"Wow, where did that come from?"

00:15:37.302 --> 00:15:40.105 align:start size:84% position:16%
-But as soon as I did,
it was gone.
-Mm-hmm.

00:15:40.138 --> 00:15:42.207
[Robin]<i> One of the effects
 of ayahuasca</i>

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:45.544
is to kind of create
a sort of chaos in the cortex.

00:15:45.577 --> 00:15:48.714
<i> That can lead
 to dreamlike visions.</i>

00:15:48.747 --> 00:15:52.250 align:start position:0%
The second time I was like,
"Oh, yeah, nature,"

00:15:52.283 --> 00:15:54.720 size:81% position:41%
and, like, "Do I feel more
at one with everything?"

00:15:54.753 --> 00:15:58.190 align:start position:0%
And I imagined trees,
but only in this ring.

00:15:58.223 --> 00:16:00.425 align:start position:0%
And all of a sudden,
they came really close,

00:16:00.458 --> 00:16:03.428 align:start position:0%
and they were all
right here in my head.

00:16:03.461 --> 00:16:06.498 align:start position:0%
But I was like,
"I did not think that.

00:16:06.531 --> 00:16:09.234 align:start position:0%
I didn't intend
for that to happen.

00:16:09.267 --> 00:16:11.403
[Michael]
<i> I think a good comparison
 for what I felt last night--</i>

00:16:11.436 --> 00:16:14.473
if you, in a sober state
of mind, just imagine something,

00:16:14.506 --> 00:16:17.309
like think of a pink elephant.

00:16:17.342 --> 00:16:20.078
Okay, now an image
probably popped into your mind,

00:16:20.111 --> 00:16:21.747
but not like
a super detailed one.

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:24.282
If I asked you
a specific question like,

00:16:24.315 --> 00:16:26.084
"How many wrinkles
are on its trunk?"

00:16:26.117 --> 00:16:27.619
you'd have to probably
imagine it again

00:16:27.652 --> 00:16:30.689
and then, like, basically
fill in that detail.

00:16:30.722 --> 00:16:33.225
But under the effects
of ayahuasca,

00:16:33.258 --> 00:16:36.728
those details were already
in these--

00:16:36.761 --> 00:16:39.598
these imagined images.

00:16:39.631 --> 00:16:42.234
They seemed only as real
as an imagined image,

00:16:42.267 --> 00:16:43.802
as a daydream,

00:16:43.835 --> 00:16:46.204
but they came with more detail,
and a few times--

00:16:46.237 --> 00:16:49.041
I'd say maybe
three or four times,

00:16:49.074 --> 00:16:54.446
<i> things appeared that I did not
 feel like I had put there.</i>

00:16:54.479 --> 00:16:56.782
But as soon as I was aware
of that, they disappeared.

00:17:00.718 --> 00:17:02.754
I'd like to look at the stars.

00:17:02.787 --> 00:17:04.590 align:start size:63% position:38%
Yeah, let's do that.

00:17:10.128 --> 00:17:12.597
<i> The morning after
 my initial dose of ayahuasca,</i>

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:14.599
<i> my head was clearer,
 and I wanted to discuss</i>

00:17:14.632 --> 00:17:16.435
<i> my experience was shaman José.</i>

00:17:16.468 --> 00:17:18.537
<i> -Hola, Michael.
 -Hola.</i>

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:20.305 align:start size:56% position:44%
[speaking Spanish]

00:17:20.338 --> 00:17:23.442 align:start size:69% position:31%
You had a perfect
introduction ceremony.

00:17:23.475 --> 00:17:25.710 align:start position:0%
Emotionally
and sort of personally,

00:17:25.743 --> 00:17:28.647
the only sort of
revelations I had

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:31.416 align:start position:0%
was that I was probably
more worried

00:17:31.449 --> 00:17:32.684 align:start position:0%
than I needed to be
beforehand

00:17:32.717 --> 00:17:34.853 align:start position:0%
and that I let that affect
my behavior,

00:17:34.886 --> 00:17:37.122 align:start position:0%
and now I'm not
as dominated

00:17:37.155 --> 00:17:39.658 align:start position:0%
by what might happen
or what has happened.

00:17:39.691 --> 00:17:41.760 align:start position:0%
I'm just kind of
in this moment right now.

00:17:41.793 --> 00:17:45.664 align:start position:0%
Like, I feel much more open
to mystical thinking.

00:17:45.697 --> 00:17:48.366 align:start size:56% position:44%
[speaking Spanish]

00:17:48.399 --> 00:17:53.138 align:start size:69% position:31%
He recommends
that you complete with
more medicine tonight

00:17:53.171 --> 00:17:55.707
so that this will help you
complete

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:57.309
the insight into yourself.

00:17:57.342 --> 00:18:00.245 align:start position:0%
Last night,
I had a third of a cup?

00:18:00.278 --> 00:18:01.813 align:start size:56% position:44%
[speaking Spanish]

00:18:01.846 --> 00:18:04.249 align:start size:69% position:31%
Three-quarters will be
the dose for tonight.

00:18:04.282 --> 00:18:05.851 align:start position:0%
Three-quarters. Okay.

00:18:05.884 --> 00:18:08.620
It's weird.
I had an intention going in.

00:18:08.653 --> 00:18:10.388 line:0%
<i> I experienced this</i>

00:18:10.421 --> 00:18:13.758 line:0%
<i> as a very interesting
 scientific endeavor.</i>

00:18:13.791 --> 00:18:17.762 line:0%
<i> But I'm fascinated by how
 I want it to have meaning.</i>

00:18:17.795 --> 00:18:21.199 line:0%
<i> I feel like I didn't hit
 that oneness yet.</i>

00:18:21.232 --> 00:18:23.435 line:0%
Tonight might be different.

00:18:23.468 --> 00:18:25.770
 [Robin]<i> Michael's getting
 the higher dose tonight,</i>

00:18:25.803 --> 00:18:29.174
and the experience
is very likely to differ

00:18:29.207 --> 00:18:33.178 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> quite substantially
 from the dose
 that he had last night.</i>

00:18:33.211 --> 00:18:36.815
 [Michael]<i> I'm interested
 in personal development.</i>

00:18:36.848 --> 00:18:40.218
I know that that's a big part
of ayahuasca

00:18:40.251 --> 00:18:42.487
for a lot of people.

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:46.558
I'm open to it, for sure,
but I do feel still

00:18:46.591 --> 00:18:49.828
<i> some apprehension
 for a larger dose tonight.</i>

00:18:56.701 --> 00:18:58.370 align:start size:41% position:59%
Hey, Michael?

00:18:58.403 --> 00:19:00.305 align:start size:72% position:28%
I'm here to pick you up
for ceremony.

00:19:07.912 --> 00:19:10.516
<i> -Buenas noches.
 -Buenas noches.</i>

00:19:26.698 --> 00:19:28.333
[Michael]
<i> The higher-dose ceremony</i>

00:19:28.366 --> 00:19:30.235
<i> was expected to last four hours</i>

00:19:30.268 --> 00:19:32.471
<i> with stronger
 and more vivid hallucinations.</i>

00:19:37.709 --> 00:19:41.346
<i> José smoked a cigar
 made of a tobacco plant</i>

00:19:41.379 --> 00:19:44.249
<i> that's indigenous
 to the Amazon called mapacho.</i>

00:19:45.483 --> 00:19:48.320
<i> The smoke is believed to clean
 the energy fields of the body</i>

00:19:48.353 --> 00:19:50.755
<i> and remove negativity
 from the ceremonial lodge.</i>

00:19:50.788 --> 00:19:52.591
[exhales slowly]

00:19:54.559 --> 00:19:57.863 line:0%
<i> The second ceremony included
 another shaman, Daniel.</i>

00:20:07.672 --> 00:20:10.642
[chanting]

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:25.523
<i> I started to see
 these very geometric,</i>

00:20:25.556 --> 00:20:29.694
bright squares, like,
stacked like Aztec pyramids,

00:20:29.727 --> 00:20:32.597
<i> moving,
 and I was traveling down</i>

00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:36.701
through these, like,
repeating kind of, you know,

00:20:36.734 --> 00:20:38.770
fractaled images of everything.

00:20:38.803 --> 00:20:40.572
I mean, too many things
to really describe,

00:20:40.605 --> 00:20:44.476
music notes and colors
and shapes and squares.

00:20:44.509 --> 00:20:46.811
<i> Then I started to feel like,
 "Oh, my gosh,</i>

00:20:46.844 --> 00:20:49.514
this is going faster and faster,
and this is too fast,

00:20:49.547 --> 00:20:51.316
and it hasn't even been
that long,"

00:20:51.349 --> 00:20:54.753
and then I felt my body being
covered with these blocks,

00:20:54.786 --> 00:20:58.890
<i> and I, like,
 saw my body from above</i>

00:20:58.923 --> 00:21:01.026
<i> and felt like
 I was disappearing.</i>

00:21:01.059 --> 00:21:02.961
<i> [José chanting]</i>

00:21:02.994 --> 00:21:04.663
<i> And that's when my heart
 started racing,</i>

00:21:04.696 --> 00:21:07.732
<i> and I said,
 "Mm, this was very bad.</i>

00:21:07.765 --> 00:21:09.034
<i> This is not good."</i>

00:21:11.402 --> 00:21:14.839
<i> A lot of emotions I always have
 were amplified</i>

00:21:14.872 --> 00:21:16.941
so loudly
I couldn't ignore them.

00:21:16.974 --> 00:21:23.048
<i> And I had to come up
 with ways to console myself</i>

00:21:23.081 --> 00:21:25.083
so that I wouldn't
be consumed by them

00:21:25.116 --> 00:21:28.353
and have a complete breakdown
and panic attack.

00:21:28.386 --> 00:21:30.922
<i> And I resisted,</i>

00:21:30.955 --> 00:21:34.526
and I successfully
brought myself back

00:21:34.559 --> 00:21:37.962
to calmness just by saying,
"I'm fine.

00:21:37.995 --> 00:21:42.901
I'm not going to die,
and everyone here can help me."

00:21:47.772 --> 00:21:50.675 line:0%
<i> The visions were really,
 really vivid.</i>

00:21:50.708 --> 00:21:52.610
<i> They didn't feel like
 they were under my control.</i>

00:21:52.643 --> 00:21:54.579
It really felt
like they were just there.

00:21:54.612 --> 00:21:58.049
A note from the song
would occur,

00:21:58.082 --> 00:22:01.419
and it would cause this image,
and that was pretty frightening,

00:22:01.452 --> 00:22:03.021
because I wasn't--
I was, like, on a ride

00:22:03.054 --> 00:22:06.758
that I didn't know
the path of.

00:22:06.791 --> 00:22:09.061
[distorted chanting]

00:22:18.035 --> 00:22:20.405 line:0%
-Robin?
-Yeah.

00:22:20.438 --> 00:22:24.542 line:0%
-I can do the EEG now.
-Yeah, sure.

00:22:24.575 --> 00:22:26.911
[Michael]<i> I spent a lot
 of the ceremony being anxious</i>

00:22:26.944 --> 00:22:29.013
about having to do
these tests with Robin.

00:22:29.046 --> 00:22:32.684
<i> I don't know how to deal
 with the lights coming back on</i>

00:22:32.717 --> 00:22:36.488
<i> and Robin talking to me
 and asking me questions,</i>

00:22:36.521 --> 00:22:39.691
<i> but the more I concentrated
 on why I feel anxious,</i>

00:22:39.724 --> 00:22:42.093
the more I realized
it was just about me.

00:22:42.126 --> 00:22:44.529
It was about how I felt,
but then I said,

00:22:44.562 --> 00:22:47.432
"I'm here to do a show.
We're filming this.

00:22:47.465 --> 00:22:48.967
Robin wants this data.

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:51.736
Everyone will be happier
if I do it.

00:22:51.769 --> 00:22:54.406
<i> So I'll just tell Robin
 I'll try my best,</i>

00:22:54.439 --> 00:22:56.174
<i> and that gave me
 the courage to do it.</i>

00:22:56.207 --> 00:23:00.111
So being less selfish

00:23:00.144 --> 00:23:03.948
basically saved me
from a panic attack.

00:23:03.981 --> 00:23:06.885 align:start size:69% position:31% line:0%
[Robin] Each time
I read an item, if you
could give me a number

00:23:06.918 --> 00:23:10.422 align:start size:66% position:34% line:0%
according to how
you see yourself
at this moment, okay?

00:23:10.455 --> 00:23:17.162 align:start size:75% position:25%
"I see myself right now
as extroverted,
enthusiastic."

00:23:17.195 --> 00:23:19.798 align:start position:0%
Um... one.

00:23:19.831 --> 00:23:21.466 align:start size:16% position:84%
Okay.

00:23:21.499 --> 00:23:23.067
[Robin]<i> This is a big change
 for Michael.</i>

00:23:23.100 --> 00:23:24.869
<i> Usually,
 he's very extroverted,</i>

00:23:24.902 --> 00:23:26.871 line:0%
<i> and on
 his pre-ayahuasca answer,</i>

00:23:26.904 --> 00:23:28.573 line:0%
<i> he gave a higher number.</i>

00:23:28.606 --> 00:23:31.843 size:88% position:56% line:0%
"Extroverted, enthusiastic."

00:23:31.876 --> 00:23:33.678 align:start position:0% line:0%
Five.

00:23:33.711 --> 00:23:36.514 line:0%
[Robin]<i> But now I'm seeing
 signs of withdrawal</i>

00:23:36.547 --> 00:23:38.616
<i> and introversion from him.</i>

00:23:38.649 --> 00:23:42.120 align:start size:81% position:19%
"I see myself right now
as critical, quarrelsome."

00:23:44.121 --> 00:23:45.424 align:start position:0%
Uh...

00:23:47.492 --> 00:23:48.993 align:start position:0%
two.

00:23:49.026 --> 00:23:53.798 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
"I see myself right now
as critical, quarrelsome."

00:23:53.831 --> 00:23:55.700 align:start position:0% line:0%
Six.

00:23:55.733 --> 00:23:58.937
[Robin]<i> The experience
 has led to a change</i>

00:23:58.970 --> 00:24:00.572
<i> in how he sees himself.</i>

00:24:00.605 --> 00:24:03.174
It's in a way reflective

00:24:03.207 --> 00:24:06.177
perhaps
of a higher waking state.

00:24:06.210 --> 00:24:08.046
[plucks notes]

00:24:08.079 --> 00:24:10.882
<i> It's interesting
 to already see those changes,</i>

00:24:10.915 --> 00:24:13.652
<i> and it's only halfway
 through the ceremony.</i>

00:24:19.590 --> 00:24:21.526
[Daniel singing
in native language]

00:24:24.262 --> 00:24:25.763
[Michael]
<i> Shaman Daniel sang in Shipibo,</i>

00:24:25.796 --> 00:24:27.499
<i> his indigenous language</i>

00:24:27.532 --> 00:24:29.768
<i> spoken by only 5,000 people
 in the world.</i>

00:24:35.006 --> 00:24:37.742
<i> I've always been frustrated
 by the difficulty people had</i>

00:24:37.775 --> 00:24:39.210
<i> in explaining
 what it felt like</i>

00:24:39.243 --> 00:24:41.646
<i> to have a psychedelic
 experience.</i>

00:24:41.679 --> 00:24:42.881
<i> Now I know why.</i>

00:24:42.914 --> 00:24:45.083
<i> It's a different
 state of mind,</i>

00:24:45.116 --> 00:24:47.886
<i> and trying to describe that
 is like trying to describe</i>

00:24:47.919 --> 00:24:50.255
<i> anger to someone
 who has never felt it</i>

00:24:50.288 --> 00:24:53.558
<i> or what colors are like
 to a blind person.</i>

00:24:53.591 --> 00:24:55.594
[singing continues]

00:25:14.078 --> 00:25:15.580
Oh, man.

00:25:15.613 --> 00:25:18.182 align:start position:0%
[chuckles]

00:25:18.215 --> 00:25:21.186
I'd say about five minutes
into that first song...

00:25:24.055 --> 00:25:26.157
I...

00:25:26.190 --> 00:25:29.027
really panicked.

00:25:29.060 --> 00:25:31.996
My heart rate picked up,
and I actually touched my chest

00:25:32.029 --> 00:25:36.000
to make sure it wasn't beating
as fast as I thought it was.

00:25:36.033 --> 00:25:38.336
But that moment,
I may have left my body

00:25:38.369 --> 00:25:41.306
or something near it
before I stopped.

00:25:41.339 --> 00:25:44.342
I was very scared
that I was disappearing.

00:25:44.375 --> 00:25:48.947
Michael is describing
what to me sounds like

00:25:48.980 --> 00:25:52.016
quintessential ego dissolution,
the start of it,

00:25:52.049 --> 00:25:54.919
that feeling
that he's disappearing,

00:25:54.952 --> 00:25:58.156
<i> that his control over his mind
 and his body</i>

00:25:58.189 --> 00:26:00.692
is ceding entirely,

00:26:00.725 --> 00:26:04.128
and he felt
some resistance to that.

00:26:04.161 --> 00:26:05.763
<i> With a high enough dose,</i>

00:26:05.796 --> 00:26:07.899
<i> you're just forced
 into that space.</i>

00:26:07.932 --> 00:26:11.069
<i> My feeling is that
 the intensity of his experience</i>

00:26:11.102 --> 00:26:14.138
was just short of that
kind of profound

00:26:14.171 --> 00:26:16.174
transformative type experience.

00:26:16.207 --> 00:26:17.775
I think he got a bit of that,

00:26:17.808 --> 00:26:19.644
but I don't think
he was all the way.

00:26:19.677 --> 00:26:22.380
[Michael]<i> I was there
 in that ego-dissolving state</i>

00:26:22.413 --> 00:26:25.049
<i> for a moment,
 and it terrified me.</i>

00:26:25.082 --> 00:26:27.385
<i> I wish I was able
 to surrender more fully,</i>

00:26:27.418 --> 00:26:29.688
<i> but I definitely
 got a good taste of it.</i>

00:26:38.996 --> 00:26:42.166 align:start position:0% line:0%
So the dosage last night
was much higher.

00:26:42.199 --> 00:26:44.102 line:0%
Yes.

00:26:44.135 --> 00:26:48.773 line:0%
Visions--
the visuals were really vivid,

00:26:48.806 --> 00:26:53.044
and the feeling of strangeness
was really strong.

00:26:53.077 --> 00:26:57.882
I'd be curious to know
what José was doing last night.

00:26:57.915 --> 00:27:00.151
What was he reacting to
that he saw in me.

00:27:00.184 --> 00:27:02.220
What plants did he call forth
and why?

00:27:02.253 --> 00:27:04.255 align:start size:56% position:44%
[speaking Spanish]

00:27:04.288 --> 00:27:07.291 align:start position:0%
He knew you were going through
an intense ceremony.

00:27:07.324 --> 00:27:10.061 align:start position:0%
It was strong for you.

00:27:10.094 --> 00:27:13.364 align:start position:0%
But he said he was very happy
because he knew

00:27:13.397 --> 00:27:16.134 align:start position:0%
this was going to have
a positive ending for you.

00:27:16.167 --> 00:27:19.203 align:start position:0%
I'm really interested
in what the lessons were.

00:27:19.236 --> 00:27:24.942
I felt so small...
and so humble.

00:27:24.975 --> 00:27:29.380
But-- but, honestly, I liked it.
I wasn't afraid of it.

00:27:29.413 --> 00:27:35.353
I was glad to be reminded
that I'm weak.

00:27:35.386 --> 00:27:37.355
I feel like the experience
amplified

00:27:37.388 --> 00:27:42.694
everything I'm concerned about
way above what would be

00:27:42.727 --> 00:27:44.762
a normal amount
to care about it.

00:27:44.795 --> 00:27:47.732
But that made my fear
and anxiety big enough

00:27:47.765 --> 00:27:50.068
that I could actually
relax them.

00:27:50.101 --> 00:27:52.170
The question is
will I remember to apply that,

00:27:52.203 --> 00:27:53.805
or will this kind of stay
in the jungle?

00:27:55.172 --> 00:27:56.941
<i> Before leaving Peru,</i>

00:27:56.974 --> 00:27:59.243 line:0%
<i> I completed one last round
 of tests with Robin...</i>

00:27:59.276 --> 00:28:01.012 align:start size:47% position:53% line:0%
I'll place this
on your head.

00:28:01.045 --> 00:28:02.747 line:0%
<i> ...in order to gather data</i>

00:28:02.780 --> 00:28:04.315 line:0%
<i> after my higher dose
 of ayahuasca.</i>

00:28:06.884 --> 00:28:08.252
-Thank you so much.
-Thank you.

00:28:08.285 --> 00:28:10.888 align:start position:0%
I can't wait to see you
back in L.A.

00:28:10.921 --> 00:28:13.391 size:88% position:44%
and see what other thoughts
you've had with these tests.

00:28:13.424 --> 00:28:15.793
[Robin]<i> Being here in
 the jungle, it's more organic.</i>

00:28:15.826 --> 00:28:19.197
<i> Because of that,
 I feel that I've collected data</i>

00:28:19.230 --> 00:28:22.467
<i> that's going to tell us
 something important</i>

00:28:22.500 --> 00:28:25.236
<i> and meaningful
 about how psychedelics</i>

00:28:25.269 --> 00:28:29.307
and ayahuasca specifically
work on the mind and the brain.

00:28:36.013 --> 00:28:38.249
<i> After returning home
 to Los Angeles,</i>

00:28:38.282 --> 00:28:40.351
<i> I had my second MRI
 so that Robin could see</i>

00:28:40.384 --> 00:28:42.386
<i> if there were any changes.</i>

00:28:42.419 --> 00:28:45.923
<i> Although my ego dissolved
 only for a brief few moments,</i>

00:28:45.956 --> 00:28:48.893
<i> I was teetering on that edge
 throughout the entire ceremony,</i>

00:28:48.926 --> 00:28:51.730
<i> and I was anxious to see what
 it looked like in my brain.</i>

00:29:00.971 --> 00:29:04.475 align:start size:81% position:19%
Robin, welcome to my home.
Thank you for coming back.

00:29:04.508 --> 00:29:07.078 align:start size:66% position:34%
I can't wait to see
what results you got.

00:29:07.111 --> 00:29:09.981 align:start size:78% position:22%
-Yeah.
-How did ayahuasca
affect my brain?

00:29:10.014 --> 00:29:14.085 align:start position:0%
Okay, so we found
something quite interesting.

00:29:14.118 --> 00:29:19.257 align:start position:0% line:91%
We found that your brain
activity became more complex,

00:29:19.290 --> 00:29:22.860 align:start position:0% line:91%
<i> more diverse, more rich,
 more varied</i>

00:29:22.893 --> 00:29:25.429 align:start position:0% line:91%
<i> under the ayahuasca
 than at baseline.</i>

00:29:25.462 --> 00:29:26.831 align:start size:78% position:22% line:92%
What does it mean to have

00:29:26.864 --> 00:29:28.332 size:84% position:58%
more complex brain activity

00:29:28.365 --> 00:29:30.501 align:start size:63% position:38%
in terms of how
I experience things?

00:29:30.534 --> 00:29:34.005 align:start position:0%
Mm, I think
we can understand it in terms

00:29:34.038 --> 00:29:40.178 align:start position:0%
of the richness of your
imagination, of your ideas.

00:29:40.211 --> 00:29:43.247 align:start position:0%
Trains of thought
can be more varied,

00:29:43.280 --> 00:29:45.583 align:start position:0%
more changeable,
more dynamic.

00:29:45.616 --> 00:29:47.518
-I definitely experienced that.
-Yeah.

00:29:47.551 --> 00:29:50.121 align:start size:66% position:34%
All right, you looked
not just at my brain

00:29:50.154 --> 00:29:52.123 align:start size:78% position:22%
through the surface,
but you went deep inside.

00:29:52.156 --> 00:29:54.025
<i> -Yeah.
 -What did you notice there?</i>

00:29:54.058 --> 00:29:56.027 align:start position:0%
We looked at a particular
brain network

00:29:56.060 --> 00:29:58.963 align:start position:0%
<i> called the default mode network
 that seems to relate</i>

00:29:58.996 --> 00:30:01.332
<i> to our sense of self or ego.</i>

00:30:01.365 --> 00:30:03.367 size:88% position:44%
<i> We've seen in other studies</i>

00:30:03.400 --> 00:30:05.403 align:start position:0%
<i> that during
 a psychedelic experience,</i>

00:30:05.436 --> 00:30:07.972 align:start position:0%
<i> that network
 is dramatically compromised.</i>

00:30:08.005 --> 00:30:10.374 align:start position:0%
<i> It shows a kind
 of disintegration and actually,</i>

00:30:10.407 --> 00:30:12.476 align:start position:0%
that process relates
quite strongly

00:30:12.509 --> 00:30:16.080
to people's ego dissolution,
and yet after the experience,

00:30:16.113 --> 00:30:19.050 align:start position:0%
<i> the network comes back
 as a kind of reset</i>

00:30:19.083 --> 00:30:21.018 align:start position:0%
<i> or a kind of rebooting
 of the network,</i>

00:30:21.051 --> 00:30:24.021 align:start position:0% line:91%
<i> and what we found your brain
 after ayahuasca,</i>

00:30:24.054 --> 00:30:26.958 align:start position:0% line:91%
<i> as predicted, was
 that your brain reset.</i>

00:30:26.991 --> 00:30:28.926 align:start position:0% line:91%
<i> The network
 became more cohesive,</i>

00:30:28.959 --> 00:30:32.263 align:start position:0% line:91%
<i> more integrated, more strongly
 connected within itself.</i>

00:30:32.296 --> 00:30:34.899 align:start size:72% position:28%
<i> Wow. Yeah, afterwards,
 I really did feel</i>

00:30:34.932 --> 00:30:36.567 align:start size:66% position:34%
<i> much more interested</i>

00:30:36.600 --> 00:30:39.337 align:start size:78% position:22%
with my identity, my past
and my future.

00:30:39.370 --> 00:30:42.240
-Yeah.
-You asked me a lot of questions

00:30:42.273 --> 00:30:45.076 align:start size:50% position:50%
before and after

00:30:45.109 --> 00:30:48.279 align:start size:53% position:47%
about my insight
into experiences.

00:30:48.312 --> 00:30:50.114
-Yeah.
-How did those compare?

00:30:50.147 --> 00:30:53.150 align:start position:0%
Well, actually we saw something
really nice in those data.

00:30:53.183 --> 00:30:56.053 align:start position:0%
So your ratings of insight
for the journey,

00:30:56.086 --> 00:30:58.522 align:start position:0%
<i> the lower dose and then
 the higher dose with ayahuasca,</i>

00:30:58.555 --> 00:31:02.393 align:start position:0%
what we saw was that
there was a graded increase

00:31:02.426 --> 00:31:04.428 size:84% position:42%
<i> in your levels of insight.</i>

00:31:04.461 --> 00:31:07.965 align:start position:0% line:91%
<i> Your score at baseline
 was 27.</i>

00:31:07.998 --> 00:31:11.202 align:start position:0% line:91%
<i> After the low-dose experience,
 it was 39.</i>

00:31:11.235 --> 00:31:14.906 align:start position:0% line:91%
<i> After the high-dose ceremony,
 it was 49.</i>

00:31:14.939 --> 00:31:17.008 align:start size:72% position:28% line:91%
<i> Wow, I definitely felt
 like the larger</i>

00:31:17.041 --> 00:31:19.110 align:start size:69% position:31% line:91%
<i> the ayahuasca dose,
 the more I considered</i>

00:31:19.143 --> 00:31:21.379 line:91%
<i> -and learned about myself.
 -Yeah.</i>

00:31:21.412 --> 00:31:23.481 align:start size:81% position:19% line:91%
Well, Robin,
I'm glad that we were able

00:31:23.514 --> 00:31:27.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
to do such a, you know,
in-the-environment-type study.

00:31:27.051 --> 00:31:30.454 size:88% position:56%
So thank you for coming all
the way out to Peru with me.

00:31:30.487 --> 00:31:32.657 size:78% position:61%
I really appreciate it,
and I hope that I helped.

00:31:32.690 --> 00:31:34.258 align:start position:0%
Yeah, it's been
a great experience,

00:31:34.291 --> 00:31:35.492 align:start position:0%
and I've learned a lot.

00:31:39.363 --> 00:31:41.265
As I look back on it now,

00:31:41.298 --> 00:31:43.567
I feel like my experience
with ayahuasca

00:31:43.600 --> 00:31:46.037
was one of resistance.

00:31:46.070 --> 00:31:48.372
<i> Instead of surrendering myself
 to its effects,</i>

00:31:48.405 --> 00:31:50.541
<i> I dipped in
 and then got scared,</i>

00:31:50.574 --> 00:31:52.243
<i> and I told myself,
 "It'll be all right.</i>

00:31:52.276 --> 00:31:54.045
<i> I'm not gonna die,"</i>

00:31:54.078 --> 00:31:56.314
<i> but I should've just gone in
 and through.</i>

00:31:56.347 --> 00:31:59.317
I did however learn a lot
about how to control anxiety,

00:31:59.350 --> 00:32:02.620
that relinquishing control
and selfishness

00:32:02.653 --> 00:32:05.990
can make it vanish,
but perhaps in doing so,

00:32:06.023 --> 00:32:08.960
I lost the chance to experience
my mind operating

00:32:08.993 --> 00:32:11.495
without the controls
and dampening

00:32:11.528 --> 00:32:15.499
I'm so used to that
I'm more comfortable with.

00:32:15.532 --> 00:32:18.369
Scientists like Robin
have managed to break through

00:32:18.402 --> 00:32:21.505
tight legal restrictions
surrounding these substances

00:32:21.538 --> 00:32:23.708
and have begun to find out
what they can teach us

00:32:23.741 --> 00:32:25.376
about the mind.

00:32:25.409 --> 00:32:28.245
Their findings so far
are just the beginning

00:32:28.278 --> 00:32:31.182
of our understanding
of these powerful compounds,

00:32:31.215 --> 00:32:34.151
which shows us how much
we have yet to learn

00:32:34.184 --> 00:32:36.554
about the mind and brain.

00:32:36.587 --> 00:32:40.024
And, as always,
thanks for watching.

00:32:42.192 --> 00:32:45.463 line:0%
[theme music playing

